  "query_preview": "..\n\nKEY MESSAGES:\n\n-  Another nice fall day before a return to unsettled weather\n\n\nA weak ridge of high pressure will continue to be over the\nNorthern Rockies today allowing for seasonal temperatures and dry\nconditions. \n\nA low pressure system will begin to push in to the Pacific\nNorthwest on Monday. Precipitation associated with this low will\nbegin to push into north central Idaho by Monday afternoon and\nthen across the remainder of the region during the overnight \nhours. A secondary disturbance will dig along the coast by mid \nweek, establishing a deep trough over the western United States. \nAnother significant low appears to move into the Pacific \nNorthwest, but the models diverge on the track of this low and its\nimpacts on the Northern Rockies. The region should be prepared \nfor temperatures running around 5 degrees below seasonal averages \nthis coming week with periods of precipitation. Snow levels will \nbe hovering around 4000-5000 feet throughout the week, especially \nduring the overnight hours allowing accumulating snow in the \nhigher terrain.",
